WEBVTT

00:01.490 --> 00:02.890
<i>Hello there.</i>

00:03.980 --> 00:05.480
<b>Ice</b>

00:05.490 --> 00:09.190
<i>A party's been formed to go retrieve 
the safe from Suori's mansion,</i>

00:09.190 --> 00:13.620
<i>so that I can turn into a giant vending 
machine and plug the hole in the wall.</i>

00:14.950 --> 00:17.960
<i>We number seven,
including Lammis and myself.</i>

00:18.520 --> 00:20.780
<i>It's turned out to be a complicated route,</i>

00:20.780 --> 00:22.470
<i>thanks to all the rubble in the roads,</i>

00:22.470 --> 00:24.960
<i>and our preference to 
avoid unnecessary combat.</i>

00:27.200 --> 00:29.960
The map says we'll be close 
once we get through here.

00:32.740 --> 00:35.610
We've finally reached a place I recognize.

00:35.970 --> 00:39.480
Yes, this alley should 
lead us to the mansion.

00:47.280 --> 00:49.250
M-My mansion...

00:51.150 --> 00:56.250
I thought I... was prepared 
to... see this...

00:57.710 --> 01:00.200
<i>To see Suori make such a face...</i>

01:00.620 --> 01:02.690
<i>I can't even find the words.</i>

01:08.240 --> 01:12.580
<i>It was the first time I've ever seen 
her bawl like any child would.</i>

01:16.050 --> 01:18.970
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:21.470 --> 01:23.290
<i>On the outside, a rectangular steel box.</i>

01:23.290 --> 01:25.280
<i>Hidden within is a human soul!</i>

01:25.280 --> 01:30.590
<i>In a world of wonder, I go to and fro 
on the back of my partner Lammis!</i>

01:26.350 --> 01:32.230
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

01:30.590 --> 01:33.110
<i>I am Boxxo! Hello there!</i>

01:33.110 --> 01:34.860
<i>That means "yes"!</i>

02:49.020 --> 02:52.900
<b>Strong Feelings</b>

02:50.740 --> 02:53.740
I apologize for losing my composure.

02:53.740 --> 02:55.730
I'm all right now.

02:56.220 --> 02:57.470
<i>Suori...</i>

02:58.240 --> 03:01.740
The safe is underground. 
Come with me, if you would.

03:01.740 --> 03:03.220
The fine art...

03:03.220 --> 03:04.180
This is horrible.

03:04.180 --> 03:06.240
Well, I expected as much.

03:06.610 --> 03:09.380
The decorations look extravagant at a glance,

03:09.380 --> 03:11.800
but they didn't actually cost that much.

03:12.240 --> 03:15.490
<i>Good, looks like she's 
back to her usual self.</i>

03:18.290 --> 03:19.500
This way.

03:20.480 --> 03:22.720
<i>A hidden basement, eh?</i>

03:24.240 --> 03:26.020
Here we are.

03:34.270 --> 03:36.520
<i>O-o-o-o!</i>

03:36.520 --> 03:39.510
<i>She must be a lot richer than I thought!</i>

03:40.440 --> 03:42.640
Look how much was saved up!

03:42.640 --> 03:45.030
<i>It's her home. Why is <i>she</i> surprised?</i>

03:45.030 --> 03:47.290
It's your first time in here, Miss?

03:47.560 --> 03:51.880
<i>I get it, Suori's never 
actually set foot in here.</i>

03:51.880 --> 03:55.680
Boxxo. You cannot accept gold bars, correct?

03:55.680 --> 03:56.540
<i>Y-ea.</i>

03:56.540 --> 03:59.180
Then I loan you all of our gold coins.

03:59.950 --> 04:02.170
<i>Thank you, S-oo-or-y.</i>

04:02.950 --> 04:05.350
My, my, you're welcome.

04:05.350 --> 04:08.430
I notice you can say my name properly.

04:09.250 --> 04:13.060
H-Hmph! You can say my name too, can't you?

04:13.060 --> 04:13.940
<i>Y-ea.</i>

04:13.940 --> 04:15.520
Say it, say it.

04:15.520 --> 04:16.940
<i>L-a-i-s.</i>

04:16.940 --> 04:19.830
You see? He said it right.

04:19.830 --> 04:23.820
<i>Sorry it's not perfect. It would 
be if I could say the "mi."</i>

04:24.510 --> 04:27.570
He isn't saying it clearly 
the way he is mine.

04:27.570 --> 04:30.440
W-Well, it's like a nickname.

04:30.690 --> 04:33.460
<i>That reminds me, these two 
don't get along very well.</i>

04:33.810 --> 04:36.980
<i>Suori was pushy in her 
attempts to acquire me.</i>

04:37.330 --> 04:39.450
Miss, we are short on time.

04:39.450 --> 04:41.590
You can have your fun 
back at the Association.

04:41.590 --> 04:42.830
Yes, I understand.

04:52.290 --> 04:54.790
This is just a loan, mind you.

04:54.790 --> 04:59.100
As soon as things settle, I intend to bill 
the Hunters Association accordingly.

04:59.310 --> 05:01.730
<i>This is probably her hiding 
her embarrassment.</i>

05:01.730 --> 05:04.910
<i>They say adversity brings 
out a someone's true worth,</i>

05:04.910 --> 05:08.110
<i>and Suori has the potential to 
develop into a charming person.</i>

05:08.110 --> 05:11.220
<i>In any case, they put in 110 gold coins,</i>

05:11.220 --> 05:13.450
<i>so my points increased by 110,000.</i>

05:13.450 --> 05:15.960
<i>That should make what's to come much easier.</i>

05:22.060 --> 05:23.630
We're back!

05:25.830 --> 05:28.010
A cold one, Boxxo!

05:28.010 --> 05:28.940
For me, too!

05:28.940 --> 05:30.190
Boxxo!

05:29.410 --> 05:31.020
Please!

05:31.650 --> 05:34.020
<i>I guess the heat's getting to everyone.</i>

05:34.020 --> 05:35.510
Gimme ice!

05:34.740 --> 05:36.320
Something cold!

05:35.700 --> 05:38.120
<i>D-Don't mob me!</i>

05:38.120 --> 05:41.650
<i>I'll give out ice cream 
and ice, so form a line!</i>

05:42.020 --> 05:45.400
<b>Orange Sherbet</b>

05:42.020 --> 05:45.400
<b>Lamune</b>

05:42.020 --> 05:45.400
<b>Grape Sherbet</b>

05:42.020 --> 05:45.400
<b>Vanilla</b>

05:48.650 --> 05:53.150
<i>That's dealt with, but this heat's 
getting worse by the day.</i>

05:53.380 --> 05:56.420
<i>The residents seem to 
be nearing their limit.</i>

05:56.420 --> 05:59.380
<i>We've got to improve this 
situation as soon as possible.</i>

06:00.130 --> 06:03.740
Let's start the meeting 
about repairing the wall.

06:03.740 --> 06:05.010
First of all, Boxxo.

06:05.010 --> 06:08.920
With the money so far, could you 
change into that giant form?

06:08.920 --> 06:12.210
<i>C-an for a b-ry-f t-igh-m.</i>

06:12.210 --> 06:14.430
How many hours could you maintain it?

06:16.300 --> 06:17.840
One.

06:17.840 --> 06:21.040
In other words, you can 
manage for a single hour?

06:21.040 --> 06:21.950
<i>Win!</i>

06:22.190 --> 06:23.400
I see.

06:23.400 --> 06:28.320
I'm thinking of assaulting the enemy after 
they do their temporary evening pullback,

06:28.320 --> 06:32.090
but if anyone has objections or ideas,
feel free to offer them.

06:33.550 --> 06:36.610
Director, I have a plan.

06:36.610 --> 06:38.240
Could we hear it?

06:39.080 --> 06:43.050
To boost our chances of success,
after the enemy withdraws in the evening,

06:43.050 --> 06:47.080
we'll move our task force into position 
near the hole, under cover of darkness.

06:47.440 --> 06:49.800
As for what happens next...

06:49.800 --> 06:51.810
If we wait for the monsters 
to launch their all-out attack

06:51.810 --> 06:54.070
on the Hunters Association 
in the dead of night,

06:54.070 --> 06:58.090
the monsters near the hole will take part, 
leaving the hole relatively unguarded.

06:58.090 --> 07:00.650
That's when the task force will strike.

07:01.220 --> 07:04.400
<i>True, this is probably the surest bet.</i>

07:04.400 --> 07:06.840
<i>But that would mean...</i>

07:06.840 --> 07:10.740
Our defenders would be exposed 
to considerable danger.

07:10.740 --> 07:11.840
Right.

07:13.760 --> 07:16.220
I suppose we still have to do it.

07:19.290 --> 07:23.080
This will probably turn out 
to be a life-or-death battle.

07:23.620 --> 07:27.700
<i>The combatants on the wall-repair mission 
task force are Mishuel, Shirley,</i>

07:27.700 --> 07:30.820
<i>the Band of Gluttons, and Yumite.</i>

07:30.820 --> 07:35.390
<i>On work detail are Shimelai, 
three earth mages, and me.</i>

07:35.390 --> 07:38.120
Boxxo's role in this is 
especially important.

07:38.120 --> 07:39.390
Do your best.

07:39.390 --> 07:40.630
<i>Lea-v i-t to m-ea.</i>

07:40.630 --> 07:42.710
<i>Honestly, this is too much expectation</i>

07:42.710 --> 07:45.340
<i>to place on a vending machine's 
nonexistent shoulders,</i>

07:45.340 --> 07:49.060
<i>but vending machines these days are expected 
to perform even during disasters.</i>

07:49.060 --> 07:50.900
<i>That means, I've got to live up to the hype!</i>

07:51.100 --> 07:52.340
Karios, Gorth.

07:52.340 --> 07:56.410
In the unlikely event we fail 
to return, hole up here.

07:56.410 --> 08:00.350
Boxxo provided a large 
store of food last night,

08:00.350 --> 08:02.400
with which you can easily last a month.

08:02.400 --> 08:06.300
Once other strata deal with their issues, 
they should send reinforcements.

08:06.300 --> 08:07.610
I'm counting on you.

08:07.610 --> 08:09.530
<i>That's what Director Bear said,</i>

08:09.530 --> 08:13.790
<i>but everyone here understood the 
likelihood of that scenario was low.</i>

08:22.750 --> 08:27.270
I don't suppose we're going any 
farther without being detected.

08:27.270 --> 08:28.310
Nope.

08:28.310 --> 08:32.810
We could kick their tails, but it's 
better to wait for an opening.

08:32.810 --> 08:34.830
<i>He's right, we have to wait.</i>

08:35.190 --> 08:37.720
<i>And have faith in our comrades 
guarding the Association.</i>

08:39.120 --> 08:42.590
I wonder if Hulemy and the rest are okay.

08:42.590 --> 08:43.860
<i>Hello there.</i>

08:44.410 --> 08:46.460
You could have just said "yeah."

08:46.810 --> 08:48.440
<i>I'm sure they're fine.</i>

08:48.440 --> 08:50.510
<i>Our reliable gate guards are there, too.</i>

08:58.010 --> 09:00.340
<i>Sounds like it's begun.</i>

09:01.320 --> 09:02.810
We've got to go!

09:03.480 --> 09:05.460
You mustn't be impatient.

09:05.460 --> 09:09.480
I understand how you feel,
but let's wait a little longer.

09:25.780 --> 09:28.300
I see the Voluptuous Figure 
is alive and well.

09:28.300 --> 09:31.790
Director, please don't call 
me by that embarrassing name.

09:31.790 --> 09:36.790
<i>If Director Bear knows it,
that must mean she used to be a hunter.</i>

09:36.790 --> 09:38.540
<i>I'd believe it, with her skills.</i>

09:38.850 --> 09:40.170
All right, Boxxo.

09:40.170 --> 09:43.400
Time for you to go in solo from 
the sky and fill that hole.

09:43.400 --> 09:44.530
Are you ready?

09:44.530 --> 09:45.800
<i>You b-e-t.</i>

09:47.660 --> 09:48.930
Boxxo...

09:49.310 --> 09:53.070
<i>I figured she wouldn't be 
happy about me acting alone.</i>

09:53.960 --> 09:55.190
Best of luck.

09:55.190 --> 09:56.310
<i>Ea-ea-ea.</i>

09:56.310 --> 09:59.320
<i>I wasn't expecting that,
and it made me respond weirdly!</i>

09:59.680 --> 10:03.330
<i>I was braced for her to lecture me
or try to stop me.</i>

10:03.330 --> 10:07.750
Grandma used to say people don't 
like ladies who are too controlling,

10:07.750 --> 10:10.630
and I've decided to have faith in you.

10:11.060 --> 10:14.090
So you be sure to come 
back in working order!

10:14.450 --> 10:16.660
<i>Lammis is showing her own growth.</i>

10:16.660 --> 10:19.230
<i>I'm really happy to have her confidence!</i>

10:19.230 --> 10:20.760
<i>Lea-v i-t to m-ea.</i>

10:23.510 --> 10:24.960
We're counting on you, Boxxo.

10:24.960 --> 10:26.220
<i>Hello there.</i>

10:32.970 --> 10:36.100
<i>I'd be waving back if I had arms,</i>

10:36.100 --> 10:38.240
<i>but this'll have to do for now!</i>

10:41.990 --> 10:47.000
<b>Kocha Kadan</b>

10:42.540 --> 10:44.390
<i>Okay, I'll be back!</i>

10:44.830 --> 10:46.310
Boxxo...

10:47.350 --> 10:48.460
Boxxo.

10:48.000 --> 10:49.210
Boxxo.

10:48.910 --> 10:51.000
<b>Reborn as a Vending Machine,
 I Now Wander the Dungeon</b>

10:48.920 --> 10:50.290
Boxxo!

10:52.420 --> 10:56.240
<i>Countless monsters are gathering 
from outside the wall.</i>

10:56.760 --> 11:00.770
<i>Still, it's surprising how 
orderly they're marching.</i>

11:01.190 --> 11:03.840
<i>Anyway, there's no time to hesitate!</i>

11:05.590 --> 11:07.220
<i>Drop point confirmed!</i>

11:07.220 --> 11:10.260
<i>Position, check!
Angle, check! Altitude, check!</i>

11:10.260 --> 11:13.930
<i>Initiating drop! Form change!</i>

11:13.930 --> 11:15.510
<i>Kaboom!</i>

11:14.360 --> 11:16.230
<b>Ice</b>

11:17.190 --> 11:20.570
<i>Huh? The frog fiends are really 
making a break for it.</i>

11:18.740 --> 11:27.870
<b>Ice</b>

11:20.910 --> 11:26.320
<i>Could that impact have messed up some 
process that was controlling them?</i>

11:26.320 --> 11:29.250
<i>If the enemy's chain of command 
is fouled up, this is our chance!</i>

11:29.250 --> 11:30.620
<b>Goods</b>

11:29.250 --> 11:30.620
<b>Inventory</b>

11:29.250 --> 11:30.620
<b>Status</b>

11:29.250 --> 11:30.620
<b>Functions</b>

11:29.250 --> 11:30.620
<b>Abilities</b>

11:29.250 --> 11:30.620
<b>Blessings</b>

11:29.540 --> 11:31.100
<i>Time to use my newly acquired function,</i>

11:30.620 --> 11:34.250
<b>Pour Hot Water
 Transaction Fanfare
 Big Winner Roulette
 Coin Conversion
 Vending Compartment Shock Absorber
 Transformation
 Telekinesis
 Change Paint Color
 Add Markings
 Switch Design
 Electric Bulletin Board
 Aroma Diffuser
 VM Installation Mount Concrete Slab</b>

11:31.100 --> 11:34.830
<i>the vending machine installation 
mount concrete slab!</i>

11:35.860 --> 11:38.870
<i>This is meant to be where you 
fix a vending machine in place</i>

11:38.870 --> 11:41.340
<i>by embedding anchors in a concrete slab,</i>

11:41.340 --> 11:44.770
<i>but I'll ignore that part,
 and activate the new function again!</i>

11:41.760 --> 11:44.760
<b>Coin Conversion
 Vending Compartment Shock Absorber
 Transformation
 Telekinesis
 Change Paint Color
 Add Markings
 Switch Design
 Electric Bulletin Board
 Aroma Diffuser
 VM Installation Mount Concrete Slab</b>

11:45.110 --> 11:49.890
<i>To support such a large object,
these concrete slabs are over a meter thick!</i>

11:50.200 --> 11:55.190
<i>The hole is about ten meters in size, so all 
I have to do is make a stack of ten!</i>

11:55.400 --> 11:57.030
<i>And the pile is done!</i>

11:58.360 --> 12:00.390
<i>Good, that worked!</i>

12:02.910 --> 12:03.790
Now!

12:03.790 --> 12:04.870
Right!

12:07.410 --> 12:08.740
Oh no you don't!

12:09.450 --> 12:11.540
<i>That's Director Bear when he's serious, huh?</i>

12:11.800 --> 12:14.270
<i>With that power of his big frame,
and those sharp claws,</i>

12:14.270 --> 12:17.660
<i>I feel sorry for any monsters 
who try to fight him.</i>

12:22.340 --> 12:23.990
Come and catch us!

12:23.990 --> 12:25.290
If you can, that is!

12:27.410 --> 12:29.560
<i>That must be the Roar blessing!</i>

12:36.180 --> 12:39.750
I'd say it's our turn now. Right, Grams?

12:39.750 --> 12:41.440
That is it, Gramps.

12:56.910 --> 12:59.260
<i>Everything's going according to plan here.</i>

13:00.460 --> 13:03.260
<i>But it feels like the monsters 
are following orders again.</i>

13:03.530 --> 13:09.000
<i>It would make sense if one of the Netherlord's 
buddies is somewhere issuing those orders.</i>

13:09.490 --> 13:14.420
<i>Typically, a commander would be 
somewhere away from the front lines.</i>

13:10.880 --> 13:12.300
Roaring Strike!

13:14.420 --> 13:17.310
<i>They'd be watching the battle 
from a short distance away,</i>

13:17.310 --> 13:20.030
<i>with some number of monsters 
stationed as guards.</i>

13:20.030 --> 13:23.460
<i>But there'd never be anyone 
who's that formulaic.</i>

13:24.010 --> 13:25.150
<i>Huh?!</i>

13:25.150 --> 13:26.490
<i>There he is right there.</i>

13:26.800 --> 13:31.660
<i>A black robe, just like how the Netherlord 
and the King of Souls were dressed.</i>

13:31.660 --> 13:33.550
<i>Doesn't look suspicious at all.</i>

13:33.550 --> 13:34.340
<i>Right-o!</i>

13:37.750 --> 13:40.460
<i>I could crush him as the 
ice vending machine,</i>

13:40.460 --> 13:44.010
<i>but if he works for the Netherlord, 
we should interrogate him.</i>

13:44.460 --> 13:47.190
<i>Okay, let's try dropping 
in as my normal form!</i>

13:50.880 --> 13:52.110
Wh-What?!

13:52.110 --> 13:54.130
<i>Huh? This guy's human?!</i>

13:54.130 --> 13:57.560
<i>I just assumed he was a skeleton,</i>

13:57.560 --> 14:01.000
<i>but I guess it's not strange at all 
if there are humans working for him.</i>

14:02.230 --> 14:04.150
What is this blue wall?!

14:04.150 --> 14:06.660
Y-You there, shatter this wall!

14:09.150 --> 14:13.170
<i>I can withstand this for a while, 
but my points aren't infinite.</i>

14:13.170 --> 14:14.510
<i>Time to end it.</i>

14:16.900 --> 14:18.060
<i>K-w-i-e-t.</i>

14:18.060 --> 14:20.820
Wh-What? Who's speaking?!

14:20.820 --> 14:22.680
<i>B-ea k-w-i-e-t.</i>

14:22.680 --> 14:27.150
<i>This is such a dumb way to talk, but 
getting through to him is what matters.</i>

14:27.150 --> 14:28.690
Stop!

14:28.690 --> 14:30.890
Wait! Stop!

14:30.890 --> 14:33.950
<i>S-to-p our-d-e-r-in m-o-n-s-t-er-s.</i>

14:33.950 --> 14:36.810
I don't know what you're talking about!

14:36.810 --> 14:39.210
<i>Yeah, he <i>would</i> play innocent.</i>

14:39.550 --> 14:43.150
<i>I guess I'll have to get 
him to want to fess up.</i>

14:50.600 --> 14:53.580
<i>Co-n-f-e-s. D-o you w-an-t to d-i-e?</i>

14:53.580 --> 14:55.830
What're you going to do?!

15:03.050 --> 15:05.830
<i>I'm aware that I'm doing 
a rather cruel thing,</i>

15:05.830 --> 15:08.380
<i>but the lives of people
I care about are on the line.</i>

15:08.380 --> 15:10.760
<i>I have to harden my heart on this one.</i>

15:13.640 --> 15:15.280
What's the big idea?!

15:15.280 --> 15:18.260
This strange taste... Is it poison?!

15:18.260 --> 15:22.030
<i>You can think that if you like, 
but you're way ahead of me.</i>

15:22.260 --> 15:24.410
<i>The real threat is yet to come.</i>

15:24.410 --> 15:25.780
That's the stuff from before,

15:25.780 --> 15:29.360
the one that explodes if you 
put it in this liquid...

15:29.360 --> 15:33.390
Y-You're not going to make me drink it?!

15:33.390 --> 15:34.410
S-Stop it!

15:34.410 --> 15:35.910
Please stop!

15:35.910 --> 15:38.170
My body will burst from the inside!

15:38.170 --> 15:39.820
<i>He's more scared than I expected.</i>

15:39.820 --> 15:45.670
<i>But there's actually no problem now that he 
drank all that cola and some time has passed.</i>

15:45.670 --> 15:48.490
<i>L-a-s-t ch-an-s. W-ell?</i>

15:49.040 --> 15:50.360
A-All right!

15:50.360 --> 15:51.850
I'll stop controlling the monsters!

15:51.850 --> 15:54.600
J-Just don't make me drink that!

15:54.600 --> 15:59.160
<i>You've shown me that the threat from an 
unfamiliar object is unimaginably effective.</i>

16:01.890 --> 16:05.140
Remove the Netherlord's bindings.

16:07.110 --> 16:10.280
N-Now my control over 
the monsters is undone.

16:12.150 --> 16:14.030
What's going on?

16:16.270 --> 16:18.290
They're acting strangely.

16:18.290 --> 16:19.790
<i>O-ver h-ea-r!</i>

16:20.680 --> 16:21.970
Master Boxxo!

16:23.740 --> 16:25.280
Boxxo!

16:25.970 --> 16:27.460
Are you okay?!

16:38.770 --> 16:41.110
Boxxo, did you do something?

16:41.110 --> 16:43.610
Who the heck is that guy?

16:43.610 --> 16:44.490
Feh!

16:51.770 --> 16:55.560
He uses a ring to convey 
the Netherlord's power?

16:56.070 --> 16:57.320
That's how it works?

17:00.780 --> 17:02.720
Points decreased by 600.

17:02.720 --> 17:04.170
<i>What?!</i>

17:04.170 --> 17:06.660
Points decreased by 404.

17:06.660 --> 17:09.210
Drop the barrier, Boxxo!

17:09.210 --> 17:10.620
If you don't, I'll...!

17:11.090 --> 17:13.920
I'll...! I'll...!

17:14.170 --> 17:18.040
<i>What's going on? This anger isn't natural!</i>

17:21.970 --> 17:23.420
<i>L-a-i-s.</i>

17:23.870 --> 17:25.590
He must pay...

17:25.590 --> 17:27.260
I'll make him pay!

17:27.260 --> 17:27.940
Wait!

17:28.460 --> 17:30.730
He's... He's...

17:30.730 --> 17:33.650
He's the one who attacked my village!

17:33.650 --> 17:37.820
He used monsters to wipe the place out!

17:38.110 --> 17:40.070
<i>So, that's it.</i>

17:40.070 --> 17:41.200
Lammis.

17:41.690 --> 17:44.600
Please, get your anger under control.

17:44.600 --> 17:49.070
Your hatred of the one who destroyed 
our village and killed our people

17:49.070 --> 17:50.580
is all too relatable!

17:50.820 --> 17:53.840
But that's why you have to endure this!

17:54.380 --> 17:57.440
The people of the other strata 
must also be suffering,

17:57.440 --> 18:02.520
and struggling hard so they 
can survive this adversity!

18:02.520 --> 18:05.470
We mustn't let them experience 
what we've been through!

18:05.470 --> 18:09.990
Put your feelings aside, so we can 
save as many people as possible.

18:13.210 --> 18:14.380
Yeah.

18:15.000 --> 18:16.330
I hear you.

18:17.000 --> 18:19.430
Sorry, Director.

18:19.870 --> 18:23.230
I'll go help repair the wall.

18:23.230 --> 18:24.380
<i>Lammis...</i>

18:28.670 --> 18:30.000
Now then.

18:30.250 --> 18:33.550
You're going to answer all my questions.

18:33.550 --> 18:35.150
I won't kill you.

18:35.150 --> 18:37.560
Rather, I won't make your death an easy one.

18:37.560 --> 18:42.020
If it's a peaceful death you want, 
you'd better give a full confession.

18:42.020 --> 18:45.910
<i>The kind, gentle Director 
Bear is nowhere to be found.</i>

18:46.320 --> 18:49.930
<i>Now he's a wild beast who'll make 
your very soul wilt with a look.</i>

18:50.650 --> 18:53.470
Boxxo, could you stay with Lammis?

18:53.470 --> 18:56.850
We'll take care of this dirty work here.

18:56.850 --> 18:59.740
It's a job best left to an old hand.

19:00.030 --> 19:01.660
<i>Hello there.</i>

19:17.330 --> 19:20.290
<i>I'm not sure what I should say to her.</i>

19:20.290 --> 19:22.990
<i>I can finally talk, in a limited fashion,</i>

19:22.990 --> 19:25.310
<i>and yet I can't think of 
anything worth saying.</i>

19:26.430 --> 19:28.730
Boxxo, I'm sorry.

19:29.760 --> 19:33.510
All this time, I've wanted 
to get revenge for Ma and Pa,

19:33.510 --> 19:36.050
and everyone from the village.

19:37.670 --> 19:42.710
That's why I became a hunter
and tried to get as strong as possible.

19:48.940 --> 19:54.310
That's why, when I saw him, 
I couldn't think straight.

19:54.880 --> 19:56.500
But that's no good.

20:08.930 --> 20:12.570
<i>No matter what happens,
I want to be on her side.</i>

20:13.040 --> 20:15.720
<i>I'll make up for anything she lacks.</i>

20:16.220 --> 20:20.560
<i>If her heart gets covered in sadness, 
I'll just repaint it with joy.</i>

20:21.130 --> 20:24.440
<i>That's my duty as her partner.</i>

20:25.360 --> 20:29.120
<i>Wi-th you to th-e e-n-d.</i>

20:30.140 --> 20:31.000
Huh?

20:31.860 --> 20:34.420
<i>I'm not sure she understood what I meant.</i>

20:34.420 --> 20:36.280
<i>I'm not going to die easily,</i>

20:36.280 --> 20:39.550
<i>so I'll be by your side until the day 
comes when you quit being a hunter!</i>

20:40.060 --> 20:42.110
<i>Or, that's the vibe I was going for.</i>

20:42.920 --> 20:44.270
Boxxo.

20:44.710 --> 20:50.130
Did you just... propose to me?

20:50.130 --> 20:51.070
<i>O-o-o.</i>

20:51.070 --> 20:53.600
<i>Whoa, wait a minute, Lammis!</i>

20:53.600 --> 20:57.960
B-But, my mother got hitched at eighteen,

20:57.960 --> 21:01.540
so ideally I'd like to 
do it at the same age.

21:00.990 --> 21:02.520
<i>Um, hello?</i>

21:02.520 --> 21:05.500
I'm happy for the offer, but 
maybe it's still a little soon.

21:05.500 --> 21:08.090
You know, we should get to 
know each other better first.

21:08.090 --> 21:09.900
Oh, and what would we do about children?

21:09.900 --> 21:13.500
Maybe I could get Hulemy to 
make some little Boxxos!

21:12.090 --> 21:15.510
<i>Um, I'd like it if you'd 
hear me out on this.</i>

21:15.510 --> 21:19.530
I know! We really need to 
reach the end of the dungeon

21:19.530 --> 21:21.260
and get you turned back into a human!

21:21.260 --> 21:26.000
I love you the way you are, but I'd 
like to see you as a human, too!

21:26.000 --> 21:28.890
Then we could hold hands and go on dates!

21:28.890 --> 21:31.440
<i>Looks like I threw her for too 
much of a loop when she was down,</i>

21:29.420 --> 21:32.380
But if we were to date, where would we go?

21:31.440 --> 21:33.390
<i>and now she's a bit confused.</i>

21:32.380 --> 21:33.420
Let's see...

21:33.390 --> 21:37.740
<i>Besides, is romance between a vending 
machine and a human even possible?</i>

21:33.420 --> 21:35.110
Oh! A field with a great 
view near where I grew up.

21:35.110 --> 21:38.180
We could bring some homemade lunches,
and have a picnic there—just the two of us.

21:38.180 --> 21:40.270
<i>Wh-Whoa! I need to calm down!</i>

21:41.050 --> 21:42.320
Just kidding.

21:42.320 --> 21:45.820
I know you're cheering me 
up because I was down.

21:45.820 --> 21:48.230
It made me feel tons better!

21:48.230 --> 21:49.520
Thanks, Boxxo!

21:49.520 --> 21:51.750
<i>She was just messing with me!</i>

21:51.750 --> 21:54.160
<i>I was this close to taking it seriously!</i>

21:54.160 --> 21:56.950
Now, time to finish up with this work!

21:57.420 --> 22:00.090
<i>For a minute there, I wasn't sure
how that would play out.</i>

22:00.440 --> 22:03.750
<i>But good! Lammis is in a better mood now!</i>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.010 --> 23:40.010
<b>The Clergyman and the Vending Machine</b>

23:35.020 --> 23:37.070
<i>You might win an extra item!</i>

23:37.910 --> 23:40.730
<i>I look forward to your next use.</i>
